2.1 GPL-3.0 section 6 - Corresponding Source for the bundled FFmpeg binaries
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The FFmpeg executable is a GPL-3.0 work and is distributed together with its
license text (section 1 of this NOTICE refers to LICENSES/FFmpeg-LICENSE.txt and
LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt, both of which are shipped with the installers).

Corresponding source of the exact build:

The bundled build's own build information is shipped with the binary in
"ffmpeg.exe.README" (copied into node_modules/ffmpeg-static/ and therefore into
the installer's resources directory). That file records:

    Version: 6.1.1-essentials_build-www.gyan.dev
    License: GPL v3
    Source Code: https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/e38092ef93
    release-essentials build configuration: ...
    External libraries: avisynth, libopencore_amrnb, libvpx, bzlib, ...
    release-essentials external libraries' versions: AMF v1.4.32, aom
      v3.8.0-180-g0eeb62d344, ... x264 v0.164.3172, x265 3.5-153-gce8642f22, ...

Accordingly, the complete corresponding source for the bundled binary consists of:

  (a) The FFmpeg sources at the exact commit recorded by the upstream build,
      https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/e38092ef93 (this is the FFmpeg
      release/6.1 branch state used to produce the "essentials" build);
  (b) the complete build configuration of that build, reproduced in full in the
      bundled file "ffmpeg.exe.README" (the "release-essentials build
      configuration" block, the "External libraries" list and the
      "release-essentials external libraries' versions" list), which is the
      configuration passed to the FFmpeg build system by the upstream build
      provider; and
  (c) the sources of the external libraries that are statically linked into the
      binary, each at the exact version listed in "ffmpeg.exe.README"
      (for example x264 v0.164.3172, x265 3.5-153-gce8642f22, libvpx
      v1.13.1-601-g655da33b8, lame 3.100, opus 1.4-9-gc8549975, vorbis
      1.3.7-10-gd84c02369, srt 1.5.3-21-g02acd18, zimg release-3.0.5-150-g7143181
      and the other libraries enumerated in that file). These are obtained from
      the upstream projects of those libraries; the binary provider is
      identified in node_modules/ffmpeg-static/README.md as listed in section 2
      above (https://www.gyan.dev/ffmpeg/builds/ for the Windows x64 build,
      https://johnvansickle.com/ffmpeg/ for Linux, https://evermeet.cx/pub/ffmpeg/
      for macOS x64 and https://osxexperts.net/ for macOS ARM64), each of which
      publishes the source and build scripts for the releases it distributes.

This repository does not publish its own source tarball of the exact upstream
build. The corresponding source is therefore obtained from the upstream FFmpeg
project and the upstream binary build providers at the URLs recorded above, and
EncodeX additionally offers, on request and for as long as it distributes these
binaries, to provide the complete corresponding source (including the build
scripts and the sources of all statically linked external libraries at the
versions listed in "ffmpeg.exe.README") for the exact binary shipped in any
given installer. Requests for the corresponding source should be directed to
developer@encodex.in.

Note on the platform-specific Linux/macOS binaries: when EncodeX is packaged
for a platform/architecture that differs from the build host, the executable is
taken from the "b6.1.1" release assets of
https://github.com/eugeneware/ffmpeg-static/releases (see
scripts/fetch-media-binaries.mjs). Those assets are the upstream FFmpeg 6.1.1
static builds distributed by the same providers listed in section 2, so the
corresponding source for them is likewise the FFmpeg sources for the matching
6.1.1 release together with the build scripts and configuration published by
the respective provider. The exact build configuration that travels with each
shipped binary is the "ffmpeg.exe.README" file (or the platform equivalent
"ffmpeg.README") placed in the same resources directory.


